WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.350
Speaker 1: Later on today, we're going to
be speaking with political scientist Rachel

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.589
Bitter Copper.

00:00:05.589 --> 00:00:10.830
And one of the questions that I will have
for Rachel is, are the numbers that increasingly

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:14.849
suggest this might not be a disastrous midterm
for Democrats?

00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:19.220
Are they numbers that can be trusted because
we're getting more and more of these numbers?

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:22.760
Now, you might remember that last week or
the week before, maybe it was.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:28.760
I told you that for the first time in this
primary season in the FiveThirtyEight forecast

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.790
for the U.S. Senate, Democrats became favored
to retain control.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:35.450
Now, it was a very small margin.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:43.290
It was 52 to 48, meaning if you run 100 simulations
with the current inputs in 52 of them, Democrats

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:49.710
end up controlling the Senate, and in 48 of
them, Republicans end up controlling the Senate.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:56.120
This is sort of like if you had a coin that
instead of being a 5050 coin was a 5248 coin,

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:03.110
meaning the more times you flip it, the closer
you'll get to 52% heads and 48% tails.

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:06.880
Now, if you only flip it once, it's either
going to be heads or tails.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:11.150
And 52 to 48 is a very, very small margin
in favor of heads.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:15.540
But the more times you run the simulation,
the closer to 52% you will get.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.330
That's the idea here.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:23.230
Those numbers have now grown to 57% in the
exact same FiveThirtyEight forecast.

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:27.200
And in fact, Nate Silver put together an article
on FiveThirtyEight, which you can check out,

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.780
which has a bunch of different data.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:32.960
The article from a few days ago called The
Political Environment Might Be Improving for

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:33.960
Democrats.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.750
And indeed, when you look at how the Senate
forecast has changed.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:43.590
If you looked at the beginning of June, Democrats
only had about a 40 to 45% shot at holding

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:44.590
the Senate.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:49.890
Remember, Democrats currently have the Senate
5050, with the vice president, Kamala Harris,

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:53.240
as the tie breaking vote in the event of a
5050 tie.

00:01:53.240 --> 00:02:02.740
Those numbers have increased, increased, increased
to where now it is a 57% chance that Democrats

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:09.259
control the Senate after the midterm elections
and only a 43% chance that Republicans control

00:02:09.259 --> 00:02:10.259
it.

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:18.610
Now, as we know, even things that are statistically
unlikely sometimes happen going into the 2016

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:19.870
presidential election.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:26.030
The odds were that Hillary Clinton had an
85% chance of winning and Donald Trump had

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:27.260
a 15% chance of winning.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.290
Now, 85% is not 100%.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:32.370
You run 100 simulations in 15 of them.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.810
Trump would come out the winner, and indeed
he did.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:39.720
This is a very, very small margin, but we
have to it's not even really come to terms

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:45.210
with it, understand that there's a unique
or at least an unlikely and uncommon opportunity

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.670
this November.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:50.480
Normally, and I know you guys are some of
you are sick of hearing this.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:57.770
Normally, when one party takes the White House
in the first midterm election, they lose the

00:02:57.770 --> 00:02:59.860
House and or Senate.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:04.819
Or if they already don't have control of the
House, they fall even further behind.

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:08.550
Or if they have control of the House and retain
it, it's by a smaller margin.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.040
You get the point.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.890
We might not see that this November.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:15.300
And if the question is why?

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:19.930
Which is to me, the most interesting question
right now, everything we know, everything

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:25.180
we can say is that it's because primarily
of two issues.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.570
Number one, abortion.

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:28.379
And number two, gun safety.

00:03:28.379 --> 00:03:34.050
Although I have to say, compared to six, eight
weeks ago, the gun safety issue is not nearly

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.640
in the forefront as much as it was.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:43.100
But we have two issues that normally are not
good issues for Democrats to run on that are

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.239
helping Democrats right now.

00:03:45.239 --> 00:03:49.740
The country mostly wants abortion to be legal
in most cases.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:57.330
We saw that on Tuesday night in Kansas, where
Kansas voters voted to defeat an amendment

00:03:57.330 --> 00:04:00.410
which would have allowed completely banning
abortion.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:03.160
They voted to defeat that amendment by a 20
point margin.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:07.069
That is not a small margin, and that's a very
red state, one of the reddest states in the

00:04:07.069 --> 00:04:08.410
country.

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:13.580
And when Roe v Wade was overturned by the
Supreme Court, even many centrists and center

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.660
right people said that this is wrong, this
is wrong.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:22.180
Abortion should be legal in most cases, and
that may not help Republicans in November.

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:23.789
In fact, it could be their undoing.

00:04:23.789 --> 00:04:27.680
And in addition to that, although I think
it's diminishing compared to a couple of months

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:33.650
ago, continued mass shootings and just absurd
reactions from Republicans.

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:36.000
Oh, it's the issue is doors.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:44.059
Armed teachers put more guns in the schools,
ballistic backpacks and bobbed grenade resistant

00:04:44.059 --> 00:04:47.529
blankets or whatever it was that was being
proposed.

00:04:47.529 --> 00:04:48.879
Outrageous.

00:04:48.879 --> 00:04:54.330
And although there are still many millions
of true believers who think the solution here

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:58.310
is more guns, certainly not to restrict access
to guns.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:04.729
More and more of the country supports all
sorts of common sense gun safety regulations.

00:05:04.729 --> 00:05:09.159
We've looked at the numbers, overwhelming
support for background checks in all cases,

00:05:09.159 --> 00:05:13.589
even personal transfers and sales gun show
every every situation.

00:05:13.589 --> 00:05:15.080
There should be a background check.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.559
And I've given you the list.

00:05:16.559 --> 00:05:21.169
But our elected officials, by and large, don't
support these things, at least not the Republican

00:05:21.169 --> 00:05:22.169
Party.

00:05:22.169 --> 00:05:28.069
This really seems to be hurting Republicans,
and this is why now in what should be a really

00:05:28.069 --> 00:05:34.599
big defeat, I mean, by all historical assessments,
Democrats should get crushed in November.

00:05:34.599 --> 00:05:38.819
It's increasingly looking if we had to just
say what's the most mathematically likely

00:05:38.819 --> 00:05:39.819
scenario?

00:05:39.819 --> 00:05:45.610
The most likely scenario is Democrats lose
the House, but not by much, and Democrats

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:47.289
maintain control of the Senate.

00:05:47.289 --> 00:05:49.190
Now, it might not go that way.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:50.309
We all must vote.

00:05:50.309 --> 00:05:51.440
We must get involved.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:53.110
We must phone, bank, all of the things.

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:54.110
Right?

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:56.460
We're going to be talking about them because
it could come down to one race in the Senate.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:58.159
It really could come down to one race.

00:05:58.159 --> 00:06:01.060
We are going to continue talking about it.

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:07.210
But the inevitable massive red wave that many
had been touting for a long time since Joe

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:10.529
Biden was sworn in that massive red wave seems
increasingly unlikely

